---
title: "object_transfer (Sui Whitepaper: Creating and Transferring Objects)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_type: Sui object operation invoked
    q_check_type --> q_transfer_addr: transfer to address
    q_check_type --> q_transfer_parent: transfer to parent object
    q_check_type --> q_share_mut: share as mutable
    q_check_type --> q_share_immut: share as immutable

    q_transfer_addr --> q_set_owner_addr: owner(Obj) = recipient address
    q_set_owner_addr --> q_return_pool: object returns to global object pool
    q_return_pool --> [*]: object accessible only by owner address

    q_transfer_parent --> q_check_parent_ref: caller supplies mutable reference to parent
    q_check_parent_ref --> q_set_owner_parent: owner(Obj) = ObjID of parent
    q_set_owner_parent --> q_return_pool

    q_share_mut --> q_set_shared_mut: ownership = shared_mut
    q_set_shared_mut --> q_return_pool_shared: object returns to global pool as shared
    q_return_pool_shared --> [*]: readable and writable by anyone

    q_share_immut --> q_set_shared_immut: ownership = shared_immut
    q_set_shared_immut --> q_return_pool_immut: object returns to global pool as immutable
    q_return_pool_immut --> [*]: readable by anyone, not writable

    note right of q_check_type
        INV-001: Object ID and Move struct type are immutable after creation
        INV-002: Object version incremented each time used as transaction input
        INV-003: Transferred object cannot be accessed in remainder of transaction
        INV-004: Move type system enforces resource safety (no copy, no accidental destroy)
    end note
